:"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pelomedusa","html_url":"https://github.com/pelomedusa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pelomedusa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pelomedusa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pelomedusa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pelomedusa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pelomedusa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pelomedusa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pelomedusa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pelomedusa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pelomedusa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-10-21T13:24:26Z","updated_at":"2024-10-21T13:25:06Z","body":"Yes, sorry. Edited.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2426676699/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"resolved"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2548187126","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98365#issuecomment-2548187126","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/98365","id":2548187126,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6X4j_2","user":{"login":"AlmightyLaxz","id":14249603,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjQ5NjAz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14249603?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlmightyLaxz","html_url":"https://github.com/AlmightyLaxz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlmightyLaxz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlmightyLaxz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlmightyLaxz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlmightyLaxz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlmightyLaxz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlmightyLaxz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlmightyLaxz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlmightyLaxz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AlmightyLaxz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-17T11:17:37Z","updated_at":"2024-12-17T11:18:51Z","body":"I have tested this and I can only reproduce the issue when using C# but not with an equivalent script in GDScript:\n```gdscript\nextends Node2D\n\n@export var StartServer: Button\n@export var StopServer: Button\n\nfunc _ready():\n\tStartServer.button_down.connect(OnStartServer)\n\tStopServer.button_down.connect(OnStopServer)\n\nfunc OnStartServer():\n\tvar peer = ENetMultiplayerPeer.new()\n\tvar e = peer.create_server(8001)\n\tif e != OK:\n\t\tprint(\"Error when creating server: \", e)\n\t\treturn\n\t\n\t# Commenting this line makes no difference\n\tpeer.host.compress(ENetConnection.COMPRESS_RANGE_CODER)\n\t\n\tmultiplayer.multiplayer_peer = peer\n\tprint(\"Server created\")\n\nfunc OnStopServer():\n\tmultiplayer.multiplayer_peer.close()\n\tmultiplayer.multiplayer_peer = null\n\tprint(\"Server closed\")\n```\n\nIt appears that any use of ENetMultiplayerPeer.Host in C# can cause the port not to be freed. Adding the following instead of Compress() in MRP.cs also reproduces the issue:\n`var peers = peer.Host.GetPeers();`\n\nAdding a `Dispose()` after using the ENetMultiplayerPeer.Host in MRP.cs seems to resolve the issue.\n```csharp\npeer.Host.Compress(ENetConnection.CompressionMode.RangeCoder);\npeer.Host.Dispose();\n```\n\nMy theory is the reference to Host isn't being let go of by C# for whatever reason and that is preventing the MultiplayerPeer from being closed with `Close()` properly.\n\nFor now, just adding something like `((ENetMultiplayerPeer)Multiplayer.MultiplayerPeer).Host.Dispose();` just before you run `Close()` on the peer seems to be a decent workaround.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2548187126/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]